  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "#Layla Haddad — Pharmacist\r\n\r\nLayla enters each prescription at her workstation, which reaches the pharmacy system over a wired connection. The dispensing unit's processor runs the mechanism that releases the pills, and a label printer prints the label. Everything sits behind the counter.\r\n\r\n### What's Going Wrong?\r\n* Prescriptions stall halfway with the bottle only part-filled, and no error message appears.\r\n* Labels come out blank, or shifted so the dose line is cut off.\r\n* The screen flickers.\r\n* All three only happen when the unit and the printer are running at the same time. All three started the same week.",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true",
